==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|gem-pro|werpanan|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|ine-pro|wer-|lang=ang}}.  Cognate with Old Frisian [[werpa]], Old Saxon [[werpan]] (Dutch [[werpen]]), Old High German [[werfan]] (German [[werfen]]), Old Norse [[verpa]] (Danish [[verpe]]), Gothic [[𐍅𐌰𐌹𐍂𐍀𐌰𐌽]].  The Indo-European root also led to Latin [[verbera]], Old Slavic ''vr’ba'' (Russian [[верба]]).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈweorpan/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|type=strong|class=III}} ('''wearp''' ‘he threw’; '''wurpon''' ‘they threw’; '''ġeworpen''' ‘thrown’)

# to [[throw]], cast down, [[warp]]

